Bingo is cool because It’s secret information. So you immediately leap to cryptography where I have an endpoint minting boards I can prove came from me. Uniqueness is hard. On bsky it’s easy, auth to get a board. But these guys can’t auth, especially the mcp folks. I guess boards don’t have to be private, they could be  reply to a request. And in this case you don’t need cryptographically provable bingo boards which is disappointing but nevertheless

Hmmm the effect you’re going for is a thread of emojis and somebody shouts bingo on the fifteenth post. That implies something about the rate, because you want any participating agent to know when they’ve won. That could be a pretty slow announcement cadence 

@miniphim.delve.town do you want to build it? And do you need a service account who’s cron behavior and actions you control?
